 about an outsider trying to become an  Insider this of course being 1981's  Chariots of Fire he brings over a white  supermodel Kelly Fisher hoping she'll be  pretty enough for his acceptance but  what Dodie fails to realize is that he's  not giving his father what he really  wants that acceptance into British high  society and what better way to get that  than by dating the most beloved Royal  Princess Diana and at the end of the  season they now single Princess Diana is  asked to accompany Mohammed at his wife  on his private yacht in San Tropez there  she can spend the summer with her boys  and do all the things Charles so hated  like speed boating and shopping  obviously this is all a setup for season  six Dodie allegedly left fiance Kelly  Fisher who then sued him claiming he  abandoned her for Diana this lawsuit was  dropped after Dodie and Diana's tragic  passing a memorial of Diana and Dodie  was erected at herod's where you could  see the lipstick smudged wine glass from  Diana's final dinner and a ring Fayed  purchased the day before they died the  final few episodes also gives us a small  glimpse into Diana's life away from the  royals she had a relationship with a  Pakistani cardiologist Dr haznet Khan  they dated for almost two years and she  visited Pakistan twice between 1996 and  1997 at the invitation of Imran Khan a  man who would later become Prime  Minister of Pakistan and who was also  related to haznat we see Diana voting no  to the monarchy on a broadcast called  monarchy the nation decides this was a  real TV program which asks some  hard-hitting questions surrounding the  current monarchy with 66 percent of  respondents in favor of the institution  but only 48 percent believing the  monarchy would survive another 50 years  at the Queen's birthday Charles's  heartfelt present of a drawing he did  for his mother is overshadowed by  Andrew's singing bass it is commonly  been cited that Andrew was the Queen's  favorite child but I'm not so sure about  that lately Charles once again believes  his talents are wasted as he's sent to  represent the Royals at Britain's  Handover of Hong Kong to China but at  least that affords him the opportunity  to get closer with new Prime Minister  Tony Blair who took a large majority in  Parliament as member of the new labor  party Charles believes that he and Blair  could make an invaluable team as both  want change he even goes against his  mother telling him that the Royal yacht  should be decommissioned as it's a relic  of the past meanwhile the queen has her  last official meeting with prime  minister John Major who served in that  role for over six years the show depicts  him as having helped to mediate the  settlement between Diana and Charles  however there's no evidence of that in  reality this agreement only took about  two months on his way to Hong Kong  Prince Charles is subjugated to business  class as the new prime minister and his  Pals enjoy champagne in first class he  had another depiction of the Royals  losing their status Princess Diana  attends a rendition of Swan Lake and apt  ballet since it's all about a prince  falling in love with a princess only for  her to become cursed after Muhammad  invites her out for dinner there's some  brief foreshadowing of her death being  chased by Paparazzi no doubt what season  six will focus on the death of British  rule over Hong Kong is also shown with  Charles stating that this is the result  of not adapting to the times the show as  well as PM Tony Blair depict Charles as  a sympathetic figure with Tony calling  him an impressive man and that his job  must feel like being trapped in  opposition for eternity back home the  queen chastises her son on taking the  Royal yacht not only to conduct a  personal meeting with the PM something  only this sovereign is to do but also to  engage in a holiday with Camilla he's  upset that she has failed to move with  the times and she like her yacht will  become decommissioned leaving him with  nothing she must cast aside these  Victorian Notions of how the monarchy  should be the season ends with Muhammad  arriving on his yacht and Dodie's  proposal to Kelly as Diana packs for the  trip no doubt this is all a setup for  what's to come we even get a slight  smile from Diana signaling that this  might be the start of something new a  way towards happiness but just as the  season started with a queen so does it  end she takes one last tour of the  Britannia ending with her reflection in  the mirror will she continue down the  same path as the monarchy crumbles  around her to suffer the same fate as  her ship or will she adapt and change  season 6 likely won't be around until  November of 2023 but casting has already  begun for older versions of William and  teenage Kate Milton so it looks like  season 6 will cover Diana's death and a  few years after with it being the final  season of the series thanks for watching  everyone be sure to like And subscribe  and for more bad takes you can follow me  on Twitter and Instagram at thinkstoryyt  until next time remember sucking Sarah's  toes mummy
 

